  "description": "Single storey\r\nrear extension: 6.00 metres deep, 3.50 metres maximum height and 3.00 metres\r\nhigh to the eaves",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Rayners Lane",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:20:58.849Z",
  "street_name": "WAVERLEY ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&nbsp; &nbsp;The proposed single storey rear extension would be within 2 metres of the boundary of\r\nthe curtilage of the dwellinghouse, and the height of the eaves of the enlarged\r\npart would exceed 3 metres total enlargement. It would therefore\r\nnot be within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A, A.1(j)(i) of the Town and County\r\nPlanning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of its rearward projection and siting, would be deemed detrimental to the amenity of the neighbouring occupiers at No. 86 and 90 Waverley Road in terms of loss of light and outlook, increased sense of enclosure and overbearing in nature. This is contrary to Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and the relevant provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
